# CODEOWNERS — paths where a change requires Jon's review before merge.
#
# IMPORTANT: there is NO catch-all `*` owner, intentionally. The auto-merge
# workflow (.github/workflows/auto-merge.yml) relies on CODEOWNERS being
# a narrow "sensitive paths" list, not a repo-wide claim. A `*` owner would
# force Jon's review on every PR once branch protection enables "Require
# review from Code Owners", which defeats the whole triple-gate auto-merge
# design for trivial rollback-safe PRs.
#
# To enforce this file, the repo's branch protection ruleset for `main` and
# `v3/main` must have "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. Without
# that setting the file is advisory only. The auto-label workflow
# (.github/workflows/auto-label-codeowners.yml) also applies
# `needs-jon-approval` on any PR whose diff touches these paths — that
# label is the hard stop for the auto-merge workflow regardless of
# branch-protection enforcement.
#
# When editing this file, also update auto-label-codeowners.yml's regex
# (patterns inlined there because GitHub Actions has no CODEOWNERS parser).
#
# Pattern rules: last-match-wins per file.
#
# ─── 2026-11-05 T1+T2 trim ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reduced from ~40 patterns to 6. Previous breadth was imported from a
# multi-tenant SaaS context (MyZone brief) and inappropriate for a solo
# lifestyle-business repo. Subagent writes to removed surfaces are now
# guarded by `.claude/settings.json` deny rules instead.
# See claude/merge-autonomy-recommendations.md §3 and
# claude/session-7-handover.md §4 for the rationale.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stripe / billing lib paths — money surface, requires Jon on every edit.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
apps/web/src/lib/billing/**                     @JDC000000
apps/worker/src/worker/billing/**               @JDC000000
apps/web/src/app/api/billing/**                 @JDC000000
apps/web/src/app/api/entitlements/**            @JDC000000

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Commercial (Stripe-touching) database migrations only.
# Non-commercial migrations are now agent-mergeable under the standard
# triple-gate; a commercial migration is the one that lands against prod
# billing tables.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
apps/worker/migrations/*_v3_commercial*.sql     @JDC000000

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CI / workflow surfaces — infrastructure of merge-gating itself.
# Bootstrap self-protect: if auto-merge.yml or sibling workflows could be
# edited without CODEOWNER review, the entire gating system is bypassable.
# CODEOWNERS itself is listed because `.github/workflows/**` does not match
# `.github/CODEOWNERS`; without this line a PR could narrow CODEOWNERS to
# nothing and then merge anything.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.github/workflows/**                            @JDC000000
.github/CODEOWNERS                              @JDC000000

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prompt-injection surface — the single doc read by every agent session.
# CLAUDE.md is kept out of CODEOWNERS post-trim because it is a thin pointer
# to AGENTS.md per repo convention; a drift there is caught by the main
# session reading AGENTS.md at start.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AGENTS.md                                       @JDC000000
